course: dictionary
lesson: 13566
title: Inadvisable: not a good idea
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words give you a warning. Inadvisable is one of them. Its clues are in its shape: in- means not, and advisable means wise or sensible. So inadvisable means not wise, or not a good idea.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. «It is inadvisable to swim after a big meal.» A big meal keeps your body busy, and swimming straight after can make you feel unwell, so the sentence warns you that it is a bad idea. Try the swap: "It is not a good idea to swim after a big meal" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You will meet this word in safety signs and formal advice, written by people who want to keep you safe. «Highly inadvisable» means an extra strong warning: it is a very bad idea. When you see a warning like this, take it seriously.
fact: Inadvisable means not wise or sensible, and likely to cause trouble.
fact: The prefix in- means not, so advisable means a good idea and inadvisable means not a good idea.
fact: «It is inadvisable to swim after a big meal.» This sentence is a warning about safety.
fact: «Highly inadvisable» means a very strong warning: it is a really bad idea.
fact: A good check is to swap in "not a good idea" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «It is inadvisable to climb on the roof.» What does inadvisable mean here? | *Not a good idea | Very fun to do | Allowed by the teacher | Easy and quick
exercise: Which word means nearly the same as inadvisable? | Happy | Noisy | *Unwise | Brilliant
exercise: Sam reads a sign: «Highly inadvisable to touch the wires.» What does highly mean in this sign? | *Very strongly, so it is a really bad idea | It means the wires are new | It means you must touch them | A little bit
test: Why would a sign say «It is inadvisable to swim here»? | To tell you the water is warm | To ask for a swimming teacher | *To warn you that swimming here is unsafe and not a wise idea | To invite you to bring a friend
test: Which sentence uses inadvisable correctly? | The sunny park is inadvisable for picnics. | The cake was inadvisable and delicious. | *It is inadvisable to run across a busy road without looking.
exam: Mum says, «It is highly inadvisable to leave the gate open with the puppy outside.» What is she telling you? | It is a good idea to leave the gate open | She wants you to buy a bigger gate | *It is a very bad idea, because the puppy could get into trouble | The puppy is inadvisable and must go to a new home
